Anyone can become responsible for a vacant home overnight. With roughly 900,000 vacant houses discussed as a nationwide issue in Japan, inheritance, distant relatives on the deed, or a parent asking “what should we do with the house?” can pull you in. This game turns that into a timeline that quietly keeps moving—property tax, decay, neighbor trouble, and the municipal ladder from advice to guidance, recommendation, order, and forced demolition (administrative execution).

The pacing and timeline feel are inspired by the web game&nbsp;*1 in 8 Billion*&nbsp;—a separate, unrelated work.

- Set starting conditions by “family-home gacha” or manual setup
- Years advance automatically (speed controls, pause, skip)
- Actions such as upkeep, consulting experts, selling, demolishing, inheritance registration, renouncing inheritance
- Multiple endings and sharing results on X

Portrait mobile UI plus a two-column desktop layout.

Disclaimer\
&nbsp;In-game tips and references to laws or programs are simplified for learning and experience only—not personal legal advice. For real procedures and decisions, contact your local government or a qualified professional.
